{
 "about": [
  "Hand shapes on the Rigify finger controls, and holds: a shape plus the left hand control's matrix in the held prop's space (the right hand mirrors it).",
  "Per finger, degrees: mcp = knuckle flexion (+ toward the palm); curl = middle and end joint flexion; dip = end joint flexion in total; spread = toward the thumb side.",
  "Thumb: rx across the palm, rz out of the palm plane, ry twist, curl its outer joints. palm: the palm control's (x, z) rotation, which cups the palm.",
  "Fitted once to contact by the ticket 28 spike (fingers closed until they touch, never refitted per exercise): goblet, grip, flat. relaxed is set by hand.",
  "Hand bone axes: X palm normal, Y wrist to knuckles, Z thumb side; the knuckle line is 14.7 degrees oblique, so handles lie along it."
 ],
